no_import_windows.description:
Recurring times where the optimiser should avoid drawing from the grid at all - shown regardless of your pricing source, since this is a site policy rather than something tied to a particular tariff. The motivating case is GloBird's ZeroHero plan (a flat daily credit if you draw under ~0.03kWh during evening peak), but this covers any similar contractual or VPP import restriction. Import is capped near-zero, not mathematically zero - a true zero could make a night with heavy load and a low battery unsolvable outright, so a small allowance is kept as an escape valve.

